  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-oh-my-terminal",
      "text": "[](LICENSE)\n[](package.json)\n\nA bottom terminal panel plugin for DSH Web GUI. Powered by `@lydell/node-pty`, it provides multi-session interactive terminals over WebSocket using xterm.js in the browser. Supports Windows ConPTY and POSIX openpty with no local compilation required.\n\n[中文文档](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Multiple terminal sessions**: manage several sessions simultaneously; a side list replaces the traditional horizontal tab bar, with right-click rename support\n- **Split terminals**: horizontal splits within the same group; a VSCode-style dropdown next to the `+` button (new / split / new by kind)\n- **Session persistence**: sessions survive panel close/reopen and are automatically restored on startup\n- **Configurable shortcut**: toggle the panel with a keyboard shortcut; integrates with the host shortcut system and the panel label updates to reflect the current binding\n- **Resizable panel**: drag the top edge of the panel to adjust its height\n- **Cross-platform**: Windows ConPTY and POSIX openpty are selected automatically by `@lydell/node-pty`; pre-compiled binaries ship with the package, nothing to compile\n- **Profile-driven terminals**: a configurable terminal profile table (type / name / path) drives new-terminal creation; profiles are auto-detected at startup and can be added, renamed, and edited in the settings UI\n- **Configurable fonts**: font family, size, and line height are adjustable and hot-reload on open terminals\n- **DSH-better-sidebar compatibility**: auto-detects"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "This package is not yet published to npm. Install directly from GitHub:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:btsd321/dsh-oh-my-terminal\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Option | Description | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `toggleShortcut` | Shortcut to toggle the terminal panel (legacy host only; see below) | `` Ctrl+Shift+` `` |\n| `fontFamily` | Terminal font family (CSS `font-family` string); empty = built-in default stack with CJK fallback | `''` |\n| `fontSize` | Terminal font size in pixels | `12.5` |\n| `lineHeight` | Terminal line height multiplier | `1.25` |\n| `terminalProfiles` | Terminal profile table (JSON array); empty = use auto-detected $PATH terminals | `''` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Terminal profiles",
      "text": "The terminal profile table is a JSON array of `{ id, type, name, path, origin }` entries:\n\n- **type**: determines spawn semantics — `pwsh` / `powershell` / `cmd` / `bash` / `zsh` / `fish` / `gitbash` / `nushell` / `custom`\n- **name**: display name shown in the dropdown menu (user-editable)\n- **path**: executable path; empty = resolve by `type` in `$PATH`\n- **origin**: `auto` (startup-detected) or `user` (manually added)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Terminal profiles",
      "text": "Auto-detected profiles (`origin: auto`) cannot be deleted and their path is read-only, but the name is always editable. The profile table is editable in the settings UI with inline editing, add-row, and delete support."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install dependencies (@lydell/node-pty ships pre-compiled binaries — ready to use immediately)",
      "text": "pnpm install"
    },
    {
      "section": "Type check",
      "text": "pnpm run typecheck"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build (esbuild, two entry points, output to lib/)",
      "text": "pnpm run build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Unit tests",
      "text": "pnpm exec tsx --test tests/unit/*.test.ts\n```\n\n> Use `pnpm`, not `npm`. Peer dependencies pin exact versions; npm's incremental resolution on an existing tree will produce ERESOLVE errors."
    },
    {
      "section": "About the build output",
      "text": "`lib/` is committed to version control. The DSH loader imports plugins as plain ESM; it does not run tsx. This repo also declares no lifecycle scripts (`prepare`, `postinstall`, etc.) because pnpm 11 rejects git-hosted packages that declare install-time scripts with `ERR_PNPM_GIT_DEP_PREPARE_NOT_ALLOWED`. Run `pnpm run build` manually and commit the output alongside source."
    },
    {
      "section": "Native dependency notes",
      "text": "Terminal capability comes from `@lydell/node-pty` (a pre-compiled distribution of microsoft/node-pty with the same API), pinned exactly to `1.1.0`. The `^` range is intentionally omitted: the package's `dist-tags.latest` points at the 1.2.0-beta series."
    },
    {
      "section": "Native dependency notes",
      "text": "It is an N-API package. Binaries are split into six platform sub-packages and shipped inside the tarball; no download or compilation happens at install time. A single binary supports both Node 22 and Node 24. Its `package.json` has no `scripts` field at all, so pnpm 10, 11, and 12 never enter the build-authorization path, giving consistent behavior across versions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Native dependency notes",
      "text": "The host side lazy-loads the package (`await import()` on first session creation). If the native binding fails to load, the error is contained to session creation; the plugin module itself remains importable and all other routes stay available."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture overview",
      "text": "```\nsrc/\n├── index.ts              # Host entry (Cordis plugin + settings + session lifecycle)\n├── routes.ts             # HTTP route handlers\n├── ws-handler.ts         # WebSocket handler (pty data forwarding)\n\nThe host side and browser side communicate over WebSocket at `/api/dsh-oh-my-terminal` and do not import each other directly."
    },
